{"id": "tea:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara:1.1.1", "source": "src:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara", "location": {"ref": "1.1.1"}, "paraphrase": "On 'then, therefore, the inquiry into Brahman', Bhāskara takes 'then' to mean after the inquiry into ritual duty: the two Mīmāṃsās form one continuous teaching, and knowledge of Brahman presupposes and is joined with the knowledge and performance of works.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:bhaskara"], "concepts": ["cpt:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "terms": ["trm:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "disputes": ["dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "notes": "Content recalled at the level of Bhāskara's known position; exact wording at 1.1.1 to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara:1.4.25", "source": "src:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara", "location": {"ref": "1.4.25"}, "paraphrase": "Bhāskara denounces those who, expounding the doctrine of māyā — disputed, cut off from its root and 'sung by the Mahāyāna Buddhists' — lead people astray.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:bhaskara"], "disputes": ["dsp:advaita-crypto-buddhism", "dsp:world-real-or-appearance"], "terms": ["trm:maya"], "notes": "The phrase māhāyānika-bauddha-gāthitaṃ māyāvādam is well attested for Bhāskara; its location (commonly cited ad BS 1.4.25) must be verified.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara:1.4.26", "source": "src:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara", "location": {"ref": "1.4.26"}, "paraphrase": "On 'because of transformation of itself' (ātmakṛteḥ pariṇāmāt): Brahman makes itself into the world; the world is a real transformation of Brahman through its power, so Brahman is both the material and the efficient cause.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:bhaskara"], "concepts": ["cpt:brahma-parinama", "cpt:bhedabheda"], "terms": ["trm:parinama-vada"], "disputes": ["dsp:brahma-parinama-vada", "dsp:causation"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara:2.1.14", "source": "src:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara", "location": {"ref": "2.1.14"}, "paraphrase": "On the non-difference of effect from cause (tadananyatvam): the effect is real and is both different and non-different from its cause, as pots from clay; Bhāskara rejects the reading that the modification is 'a mere name' in the sense of being unreal.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:bhaskara"], "concepts": ["cpt:brahma-parinama", "cpt:bhedabheda"], "disputes": ["dsp:brahma-parinama-vada", "dsp:world-real-or-appearance"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara:2.3.43", "source": "src:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara", "location": {"ref": "2.3.43"}, "paraphrase": "On the soul as a part (aṃśa) of Brahman: the soul is a part of Brahman, different from it by its limiting adjuncts (upādhi) — the intellect and the rest, which are real — and non-different from it by nature (aupādhika-bhedābheda).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:bhaskara"], "concepts": ["cpt:aupadhika-bhedabheda", "cpt:jiva-as-part-of-brahman"], "terms": ["trm:upadhi", "trm:amsa", "trm:aupadhika-bhedabheda"], "disputes": ["dsp:aupadhika-vs-svabhavika-bhedabheda", "dsp:souls-one-or-distinct"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara:4.1", "source": "src:brahma-sutra-bhasya-bhaskara", "location": {"ref": "4.1"}, "paraphrase": "Bhāskara holds that liberation is not attained while the body lasts: the embodied knower still bears real adjuncts; knowledge combined with prescribed works continues until death, after which the soul, freed of adjuncts, becomes non-different from Brahman.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "action"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "death-dying"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:bhaskara"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti", "cpt:moksa", "cpt:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "disputes": ["dsp:jivanmukti", "dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "notes": "Pāda-level reference (BS 4.1, esp. 4.1.13–19); exact sūtra to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
